<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">My&nbsp;thoughts</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The dead/alive swap is likely correct, but there's still unanswered questions. For starters, some of the traits in the bullet points don't line up with that effect: why would it have a size (which are one dimensional units for that matter), why would it be a &quot;space-time aberration&quot;, and how would there be &quot;instances&quot; of the SCP if the SCP is the memetic effect itself and not its infectees? Are some of the &quot;surviving&quot; researchers lying or mistaken? Doctor Walters claimed it was ectoentropic, had particular instances and was a space time aberration, none of which makes any sense with the dead/alive swap effect.</p>
<p>Why can't/won't any of them disclose the traitor? What did the traitor do in the first place?</p>
<p>There's a weird line in the containment procedures, &quot;The guilty party is to be executed, the method of termination is currently undecided&quot;. The termination procedure is unimportant for a supposedly alive non-anomalous person, so I think the author of the document is aware of the effect and is unsure how to actually &quot;execute&quot; a dead person!</p>
